These are some minor bug fixes for Nethack 3.1.0.

-When blind how can you tel lif a monster is invisible, infact if you
have see invisible how could you tell at all.  However once a monster is
identified as invisible it *should* really stay noted as invisible I
guess?!

-When attacking a pudding you can some times get a message some how you
missed (also when you are a pudding although being a blind creature
there is no way to get any messages :).  However passive attacks
(rusting) and dividing still occur.  The fix below fixes the dividing,
the passive attacks still occur if you attack a pudding.  Major mods are
really required in uhit.c to stop passive attacks.

-Finally a cosmetic change so that Olog-hai and Uruk-hai dont get an 's'
added to the end for plural.


enjoy,
bernard.

diff ../bak/src/do_name.c do_name.c
481c481
< 	if (mtmp->minvis)
---
> 	if (mtmp->minvis && !Blind)


diff ../bak/src/mhitu.c mhitu.c
782a783
> 			if (!dmg) break;    /* somehow you missed! */
1282,1284c1283,1288
< 	res = passiveum(olduasmon, mtmp, mattk);
< 	stop_occupation();
< 	return res;
---
> 	if (dmg) {
> 	   res = passiveum(olduasmon, mtmp, mattk);
> 	   stop_occupation();
> 	   return res;
> 	}
> 	else return 1;

diff ../bak/src/objnam.c objnam.c
907c907
< 	if ((len >= 7 && !strcmp(spot-6, "samurai")) ||
---
> 	if ((len >= 2 && !strcmp(spot-1, "ai")) || /* samurai, Uruk-hai */

